IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `scja1-part3-div7-9`

-- Tests for scja1-part3-div7-9.l4 (ss 29 to 29E). Expected values are written from the text (SCJA1969.txt lines 2040-2306), not from the code.
-- Weekdays used below, checked against a calendar: 1 June 2024 is a Saturday, 3 June 2024 a Monday, 16 June 2024 a Sunday, 17 June 2024 a Monday, 18 June 2024 a Tuesday.

§ `Fixtures`

-- A decision with the fields these sections turn on: the court, the jurisdiction exercised, the nature of the proceeding, made after a trial, the amount in dispute, the date made, the date the judgment or order was extracted,
-- and whether a written law provides that it is final or that no appeal lies.
GIVEN `made by` IS A Court
      jurisdiction IS A `Jurisdiction exercised`
      nature IS A `Nature of the proceeding`
      `after a trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      amount IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `date made` IS A DATE
      extracted IS A MAYBE DATE
      `final by a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Decision
`a decision` MEANS Decision OF `made by`, jurisdiction, nature, `any other civil matter`, (Order OF `another order or application`, `granted unconditionally`), `after a trial`, FALSE, amount, `date made`, extracted, `final by a written law`, FALSE

-- the ordinary case: a General Division civil decision in its original jurisdiction, not after a trial, with the amount in dispute given, made on Monday 3 June 2024, not yet extracted
GIVEN amount IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A Decision
`a General Division civil decision` MEANS `a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding` FALSE amount (Date 3 6 2024) NOTHING FALSE

`a decision of the General Division on appeal` MEANS `a decision` `General Division` `appellate jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding` FALSE (JUST 1000) (Date 3 6 2024) NOTHING FALSE

`a decision made after a trial` MEANS `a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding` TRUE (JUST 1000) (Date 3 6 2024) NOTHING FALSE

-- made on Saturday 1 June 2024, so that the 15th day after it falls on a Sunday
`a decision made on a Saturday` MEANS `a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding` FALSE (JUST 1000) (Date 1 6 2024) NOTHING FALSE

`a decision with the judgment extracted on 10 June` MEANS `a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding` FALSE (JUST 1000) (Date 3 6 2024) (JUST (Date 10 6 2024)) FALSE

`a decision with the judgment extracted on 20 June` MEANS `a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding` FALSE (JUST 1000) (Date 3 6 2024) (JUST (Date 20 6 2024)) FALSE

`a decision of the SICC` MEANS `a decision` `Singapore International Commercial Court` `original jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding` FALSE (JUST 1000) (Date 3 6 2024) NOTHING TRUE

`a decision of a District Court` MEANS `a decision` `District Court` `original jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding` FALSE (JUST 1000) (Date 3 6 2024) NOTHING TRUE

`a supervisory decision of the General Division` MEANS `a decision` `General Division` `supervisory and revisionary jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding` FALSE (JUST 1000) (Date 3 6 2024) NOTHING TRUE

`a criminal decision of the General Division` MEANS `a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `a criminal proceeding` FALSE (JUST 1000) (Date 3 6 2024) NOTHING TRUE

`a decision a written law makes final` MEANS `a decision` `General Division` `original jurisdiction` `a civil proceeding` FALSE (JUST 1000) (Date 3 6 2024) NOTHING TRUE

`no public holidays` MEANS EMPTY
`17 June 2024 is a public holiday` MEANS LIST Date 17 6 2024

§§ `The scope shared by ss 29, 29A and 29C`

#ASSERT `ss 29, 29A and 29C the decision is of the General Division in its original or appellate civil jurisdiction` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000))
#ASSERT `ss 29, 29A and 29C the decision is of the General Division in its original or appellate civil jurisdiction` `a decision of the General Division on appeal`
#ASSERT NOT (`ss 29, 29A and 29C the decision is of the General Division in its original or appellate civil jurisdiction` `a supervisory decision of the General Division`)
#ASSERT NOT (`ss 29, 29A and 29C the decision is of the General Division in its original or appellate civil jurisdiction` `a criminal decision of the General Division`)
#ASSERT NOT (`ss 29, 29A and 29C the decision is of the General Division in its original or appellate civil jurisdiction` `a decision of a District Court`)

§§ `s 29: no appeal in certain cases`

-- JUST TRUE means "an appeal cannot be brought". Inputs: the decision, the Fourth Schedule's answer (seam 4)
#ASSERT (`s 29 an appeal cannot be brought against the decision` `a decision a written law makes final` NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29 an appeal cannot be brought against the decision` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the Fourth Schedule does not say no appeal can be brought: the section does not decide
#ASSERT (`s 29 an appeal cannot be brought against the decision` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29 an appeal cannot be brought against the decision` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29 an appeal cannot be brought against the decision` `a decision of the General Division on appeal` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a decision outside the section's scope
#ASSERT (`s 29 an appeal cannot be brought against the decision` `a supervisory decision of the General Division` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29 an appeal cannot be brought against the decision` `a decision of a District Court` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a decision of the Singapore International Commercial Court (fork K1)
#ASSERT (`s 29 an appeal cannot be brought against the decision` `a decision of the SICC` (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 29A: permission required to appeal`

-- (1)(b): the Act's own figure is $250,000: at the figure, within; one dollar over, outside
#ASSERT (`s 29A(1)(b) the amount in dispute or value of the subject matter does not exceed the sum` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 250000)) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29A(1)(b) the amount in dispute or value of the subject matter does not exceed the sum` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 249999)) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29A(1)(b) the amount in dispute or value of the subject matter does not exceed the sum` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 250001)) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 29A(1)(b) the amount in dispute or value of the subject matter does not exceed the sum` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 0)) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an order under (3) raising the sum to $500,000 and one lowering it to $100,000
#ASSERT (`s 29A(1)(b) the amount in dispute or value of the subject matter does not exceed the sum` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 400000)) (JUST 500000)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29A(1)(b) the amount in dispute or value of the subject matter does not exceed the sum` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 500001)) (JUST 500000)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 29A(1)(b) the amount in dispute or value of the subject matter does not exceed the sum` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 150000)) (JUST 100000)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no amount or value: the Act does not say how an unvalued case counts
#ASSERT (`s 29A(1)(b) the amount in dispute or value of the subject matter does not exceed the sum` (`a General Division civil decision` NOTHING) NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING

-- (1): inputs are the decision, a written law expressly provides permission, the order's sum, seam 5 (an exception to (b)), seam 6 (the case is one in paragraph 3, 4(1) or 5(1) and no exception applies)
#ASSERT (`s 29A(1) permission is required before an appeal may be brought against the decision` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) TRUE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) met, and the Fifth Schedule has no exception: permission is required
#ASSERT (`s 29A(1) permission is required before an appeal may be brought against the decision` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 250000)) FALSE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29A(1) permission is required before an appeal may be brought against the decision` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 100)) FALSE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- one dollar over the figure: (b) is not met, and with (a) and (c) not met the Act does not say
#ASSERT (`s 29A(1) permission is required before an appeal may be brought against the decision` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 250001)) FALSE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b) met but the Fifth Schedule's exception takes the case out
#ASSERT (`s 29A(1) permission is required before an appeal may be brought against the decision` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) FALSE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b) met but the Fifth Schedule's answer on exceptions is not given
#ASSERT (`s 29A(1) permission is required before an appeal may be brought against the decision` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) FALSE NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (c): a case in paragraph 3, 4(1) or 5(1) with no exception applying, whatever the amount
#ASSERT (`s 29A(1) permission is required before an appeal may be brought against the decision` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 9000000)) FALSE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the amount is not valued, (b) not decided, and (c) not met
#ASSERT (`s 29A(1) permission is required before an appeal may be brought against the decision` (`a General Division civil decision` NOTHING) FALSE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the sum raised by an order under (3): $400,000 within $500,000
#ASSERT (`s 29A(1) permission is required before an appeal may be brought against the decision` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 400000)) FALSE (JUST 500000) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- outside the section's scope
#ASSERT (`s 29A(1) permission is required before an appeal may be brought against the decision` `a decision of a District Court` TRUE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29A(1) permission is required before an appeal may be brought against the decision` `a decision of the SICC` TRUE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29A(1) permission is required before an appeal may be brought against the decision` `a supervisory decision of the General Division` TRUE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2): inputs are the court a written law specifies, the Fifth Schedule's court (seam 7)
#ASSERT (`s 29A(2) the court from which permission must be obtained` (JUST `Court of Appeal`) (JUST `Appellate Division`)) EQUALS JUST `Court of Appeal`
#ASSERT (`s 29A(2) the court from which permission must be obtained` NOTHING (JUST `Appellate Division`)) EQUALS JUST `Appellate Division`
#ASSERT (`s 29A(2) the court from which permission must be obtained` NOTHING (JUST `General Division`)) EQUALS JUST `General Division`
-- neither names a court
#ASSERT (`s 29A(2) the court from which permission must be obtained` NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the yes/no twin: inputs are the court asked about, the written law's court, the Fifth Schedule's court
#ASSERT (`s 29A(2) permission must be obtained from this court` `Appellate Division` NOTHING (JUST `Appellate Division`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29A(2) permission must be obtained from this court` `General Division` NOTHING (JUST `Appellate Division`)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 29A(2) permission must be obtained from this court` `Court of Appeal` (JUST `Court of Appeal`) (JUST `Appellate Division`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29A(2) permission must be obtained from this court` `Appellate Division` (JUST `Court of Appeal`) (JUST `Appellate Division`)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 29A(2) permission must be obtained from this court` `Appellate Division` NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3)
#ASSERT (`s 29A(3) the President may specify another sum in substitution of the sum mentioned in section 29A(1)(b)` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29A(3) the President may specify another sum in substitution of the sum mentioned in section 29A(1)(b)` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29A(3) the President may specify another sum in substitution of the sum mentioned in section 29A(1)(b)` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29A(3) the President may specify another sum in substitution of the sum mentioned in section 29A(1)(b)` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 29B: further arguments before notice of appeal is filed`

-- (1): inputs are the decision, made by a Judge
#ASSERT (`s 29B(1) this section applies to the decision` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29B(1) this section applies to the decision` `a decision of the General Division on appeal` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- after a trial of an action: the text excludes it
#ASSERT (`s 29B(1) this section applies to the decision` `a decision made after a trial` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not made by a Judge (the Registrar)
#ASSERT (`s 29B(1) this section applies to the decision` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29B(1) this section applies to the decision` `a decision of a District Court` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29B(1) this section applies to the decision` `a supervisory decision of the General Division` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29B(1) this section applies to the decision` `a decision of the SICC` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2)(b): the 15th day after the date on which the decision is made. Decision on Monday 3 June 2024: the 15th day is Tuesday 18 June 2024
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the 15th day after the date on which the decision is made` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST (Date 18 6 2024)
-- decision on Saturday 1 June 2024: the 15th day is Sunday 16 June, so the period includes Monday 17 June (Interpretation Act s 50(b))
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the 15th day after the date on which the decision is made` `a decision made on a Saturday` `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST (Date 17 6 2024)
-- Monday 17 June 2024 a public holiday as well: Tuesday 18 June
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the 15th day after the date on which the decision is made` `a decision made on a Saturday` `17 June 2024 is a public holiday`) EQUALS JUST (Date 18 6 2024)
-- the day before which the request must be made: the earlier of (a) extraction and (b) the 15th day
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the day before which the request for further arguments must be made` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST (Date 18 6 2024)
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the day before which the request for further arguments must be made` `a decision with the judgment extracted on 10 June` `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 6 2024)
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the day before which the request for further arguments must be made` `a decision with the judgment extracted on 20 June` `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST (Date 18 6 2024)

-- the twin, reading 1: inputs are the decision, the date of the request, the public holidays. No extraction yet: before the 15th day (18 June) means 17 June at the latest
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the request for further arguments is made before the earlier of the following` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) (Date 3 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the request for further arguments is made before the earlier of the following` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) (Date 17 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the request for further arguments is made before the earlier of the following` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) (Date 18 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the request for further arguments is made before the earlier of the following` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) (Date 19 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- extracted on 10 June: a request before it is in time, on it is undecided (the core holds the date, not the time), after it is out of time
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the request for further arguments is made before the earlier of the following` `a decision with the judgment extracted on 10 June` (Date 9 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the request for further arguments is made before the earlier of the following` `a decision with the judgment extracted on 10 June` (Date 10 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the request for further arguments is made before the earlier of the following` `a decision with the judgment extracted on 10 June` (Date 11 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- extracted on 20 June, after the 15th day: the earlier is the 15th day
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the request for further arguments is made before the earlier of the following` `a decision with the judgment extracted on 20 June` (Date 17 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the request for further arguments is made before the earlier of the following` `a decision with the judgment extracted on 20 June` (Date 18 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- decision on Saturday 1 June: the 15th day is moved to Monday 17 June, so Sunday 16 June is in time and 17 June is not
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the request for further arguments is made before the earlier of the following` `a decision made on a Saturday` (Date 16 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the request for further arguments is made before the earlier of the following` `a decision made on a Saturday` (Date 17 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the request for further arguments is made before the earlier of the following` `a decision made on a Saturday` (Date 17 6 2024) `17 June 2024 is a public holiday`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the other reading of "before the 15th day": the 15th day itself counts
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) other reading: the request is made on or before the 15th day after the date on which the decision is made` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) (Date 18 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) other reading: the request is made on or before the 15th day after the date on which the decision is made` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) (Date 19 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) other reading: the request is made on or before the 15th day after the date on which the decision is made` `a decision with the judgment extracted on 10 June` (Date 9 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) other reading: the request is made on or before the 15th day after the date on which the decision is made` `a decision with the judgment extracted on 10 June` (Date 10 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) other reading: the request is made on or before the 15th day after the date on which the decision is made` `a decision with the judgment extracted on 10 June` (Date 11 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (2) as a whole: inputs are the decision, made by a Judge, a notice of appeal already filed, a request by a party or the Judge, the date of the request, the public holidays
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the Judge who made the decision may hear further arguments in respect of the decision` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 10 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a notice of appeal has already been filed
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the Judge who made the decision may hear further arguments in respect of the decision` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 10 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- nobody requested
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the Judge who made the decision may hear further arguments in respect of the decision` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 10 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the request is late
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the Judge who made the decision may hear further arguments in respect of the decision` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 18 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a decision after a trial: the section does not apply
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the Judge who made the decision may hear further arguments in respect of the decision` `a decision made after a trial` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 10 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not made by a Judge
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the Judge who made the decision may hear further arguments in respect of the decision` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 10 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the request on the extraction day is undecided
#ASSERT (`s 29B(2) the Judge who made the decision may hear further arguments in respect of the decision` `a decision with the judgment extracted on 10 June` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 10 6 2024) `no public holidays`) EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3): inputs are the Judge has heard further arguments, the step
#ASSERT (`s 29B(3) the Judge may take the step` TRUE `s 29B(3) affirm the decision`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29B(3) the Judge may take the step` TRUE `s 29B(3) vary the decision`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29B(3) the Judge may take the step` TRUE `s 29B(3) set aside the decision`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29B(3) the Judge may take the step` TRUE `s 29B(3) take another step`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29B(3) the Judge may take the step` FALSE `s 29B(3) affirm the decision`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4): the subsection applies where a request has been made
#ASSERT (`s 29B(4) this subsection applies` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29B(4) this subsection applies` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4)(a): the bar, JUST TRUE meaning a notice of appeal may not yet be filed. Inputs: a request made, the Judge has affirmed/varied/set aside, the Judge has certified or is deemed to have certified
#ASSERT (`s 29B(4)(a) a notice of appeal may not be filed against the decision yet` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29B(4)(a) a notice of appeal may not be filed against the decision yet` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 29B(4)(a) a notice of appeal may not be filed against the decision yet` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 29B(4)(a) a notice of appeal may not be filed against the decision yet` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4)(b): inputs are a request made, the date the Judge affirmed/varied/set aside, the date the Judge certified
#ASSERT (`s 29B(4)(b) the date on which the time for filing a notice of appeal begins` TRUE (JUST (Date 1 7 2024)) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 7 2024)
#ASSERT (`s 29B(4)(b) the date on which the time for filing a notice of appeal begins` TRUE NOTHING (JUST (Date 2 7 2024))) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 7 2024)
-- both events are given: the Act does not say which controls
#ASSERT (`s 29B(4)(b) the date on which the time for filing a notice of appeal begins` TRUE (JUST (Date 1 7 2024)) (JUST (Date 2 7 2024))) EQUALS NOTHING
-- neither event has happened: the time has not begun
#ASSERT (`s 29B(4)(b) the date on which the time for filing a notice of appeal begins` TRUE NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- no request was made: the subsection does not apply
#ASSERT (`s 29B(4)(b) the date on which the time for filing a notice of appeal begins` FALSE (JUST (Date 1 7 2024)) NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5)
#ASSERT (`s 29B(5) a party to the hearing may request further arguments before filing a notice of appeal` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29B(5) a party to the hearing may request further arguments before filing a notice of appeal` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29B(5) a party to the hearing is required to request further arguments before filing a notice of appeal` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 29B(5) a party to the hearing is required to request further arguments before filing a notice of appeal` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 29C: the court to which the appeal is to be made`

-- (2): inputs are the decision, the Sixth Schedule's answer (seam 8), another written law provides the Court of Appeal
#ASSERT (`s 29C(2) the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) (JUST TRUE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29C(2) the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) (JUST FALSE) TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29C(2) the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) NOTHING TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- neither the Sixth Schedule nor another written law provides it: "if ... so provides" is not met
#ASSERT (`s 29C(2) the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) (JUST FALSE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the Sixth Schedule's answer is not given and no other written law provides it
#ASSERT (`s 29C(2) the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) NOTHING FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a decision of a District Court is not an appeal against a decision of the General Division, so s 29C(2) does not speak of it even when the Schedule input is JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29C(2) the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `a decision of a District Court` (JUST TRUE) TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Sixth Schedule input JUST TRUE (the Schedule is understood to name the SICC): the Schedule's own answer holds for an SICC decision, so fork K1 does not bite
#ASSERT (`s 29C(2) the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `a decision of the SICC` (JUST TRUE) TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29C(2) the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `a decision of the SICC` (JUST TRUE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Sixth Schedule input NOTHING with an SICC decision: it stays NOTHING, whether or not another written law is said to provide it (fork K1)
#ASSERT (`s 29C(2) the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `a decision of the SICC` NOTHING FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29C(2) the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `a decision of the SICC` NOTHING TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29C(2) the appeal is to be made to the Court of Appeal` `a decision of the SICC` (JUST FALSE) TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1)
#ASSERT (`s 29C(1) the appeal is to be made to the Appellate Division` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) (JUST FALSE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29C(1) the appeal is to be made to the Appellate Division` `a decision of the General Division on appeal` (JUST FALSE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29C(1) the appeal is to be made to the Appellate Division` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) (JUST TRUE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 29C(1) the appeal is to be made to the Appellate Division` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) (JUST FALSE) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 29C(1) the appeal is to be made to the Appellate Division` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) NOTHING FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29C(1) the appeal is to be made to the Appellate Division` `a decision of a District Court` (JUST FALSE) FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29C(1) the appeal is to be made to the Appellate Division` `a decision of the SICC` (JUST FALSE) FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29C(1) the appeal is to be made to the Appellate Division` `a decision of the SICC` (JUST TRUE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the court answer (seam 9)
#ASSERT (`s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) (JUST FALSE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST `Appellate Division`
#ASSERT (`s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) (JUST TRUE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST `Court of Appeal`
#ASSERT (`s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) (JUST FALSE) TRUE) EQUALS JUST `Court of Appeal`
#ASSERT (`s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made` (`a General Division civil decision` (JUST 1000)) NOTHING FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made` `a decision of a District Court` (JUST FALSE) FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made` `a decision of the SICC` (JUST FALSE) FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made` `a decision of the SICC` (JUST TRUE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST `Court of Appeal`
#ASSERT (`s 29C the court to which the appeal is to be made` `a decision of the SICC` NOTHING FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3)
#ASSERT (`s 29C(3) section 29C creates a right of appeal against the decision` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 29C(3) section 29C creates a right of appeal against the decision` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 29D: power to transfer an appeal to the Court of Appeal`

-- (1): inputs are the appeal, an order under section 39A of the Land Acquisition Act 1966 is in force
#ASSERT (`s 29D(1) the Court of Appeal may transfer the appeal to itself` `s 29D(1)(a) an appeal against a decision of the General Division that has been made to the Appellate Division` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29D(1) the Court of Appeal may transfer the appeal to itself` `s 29D(1)(b) an appeal made to the Appellate Division under section 29(2) or 38(2) of the Land Acquisition Act 1966` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29D(1) the Court of Appeal may transfer the appeal to itself` `s 29D(1)(b) an appeal made to the Appellate Division under section 29(2) or 38(2) of the Land Acquisition Act 1966` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 29D(1) the Court of Appeal may transfer the appeal to itself` `s 29D(1) another appeal` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): inputs are the way, the ground (i), the ground (ii)
#ASSERT (`s 29D(2) the power in section 29D(1) may be exercised in this way` `s 29D(2)(a) on its own motion` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29D(2) the power in section 29D(1) may be exercised in this way` `s 29D(2)(b) on a reference by the Appellate Division` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29D(2) the power in section 29D(1) may be exercised in this way` `s 29D(2)(c) on an application to the Court of Appeal by a party to the appeal` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29D(2) the power in section 29D(1) may be exercised in this way` `s 29D(2)(c) on an application to the Court of Appeal by a party to the appeal` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "may only be made" on those two grounds
#ASSERT (`s 29D(2) the power in section 29D(1) may be exercised in this way` `s 29D(2)(c) on an application to the Court of Appeal by a party to the appeal` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3)
#ASSERT (`s 29D(3) the Court of Appeal is to have regard to the matter` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29D(3) the Court of Appeal is to have regard to the matter` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29D(3) the Court of Appeal is to have regard to the matter` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4), (5)
#ASSERT (`s 29D(4) the Rules of Court may prescribe different matters for the circumstance` `s 29D(2)(a) on its own motion`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29D(4) the Rules of Court may prescribe different matters for the circumstance` `s 29D(2)(b) on a reference by the Appellate Division`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29D(4) the Rules of Court may prescribe different matters for the circumstance` `s 29D(2)(c) on an application to the Court of Appeal by a party to the appeal`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29D(5) the appeal may be transferred under section 29D(1) even though it was made in accordance with section 29C(1)` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29D(5) the appeal may be transferred under section 29D(1) even though it was made in accordance with section 29C(1)` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

-- The regulative rule for s 29D(3), run: a Court of Appeal that has regard is FULFILLED; one that decides without having that regard leaves the duty standing (the section sets no time);
-- where (3) does not apply the rule is FULFILLED at once. (Read from the output of `l4 run`: FULFILLED, a residual MUST, FULFILLED.)
#TRACE `s 29D(3) the Court of Appeal must have regard to the matter prescribed by the Rules of Court` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 29D(3) the Court of Appeal` DOES `s 29D(3) has regard to the matter prescribed by the Rules of Court` AT 1
#TRACE `s 29D(3) the Court of Appeal must have regard to the matter prescribed by the Rules of Court` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 29D(3) the Court of Appeal` DOES `s 29D(3) decides without having that regard` AT 1
#TRACE `s 29D(3) the Court of Appeal must have regard to the matter prescribed by the Rules of Court` FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 29D(3) the Court of Appeal` DOES `s 29D(3) decides without having that regard` AT 1

§§ `s 29E: power to transfer an appeal to the Appellate Division`

#ASSERT (`s 29E(1) the Court of Appeal may transfer the appeal to the Appellate Division` `s 29E(1)(a) an appeal against a decision of the General Division in a civil cause or matter, in its original or appellate civil jurisdiction, that has been made to the Court of Appeal`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29E(1) the Court of Appeal may transfer the appeal to the Appellate Division` `s 29E(1)(b) an appeal made to the Court of Appeal under section 29(2) or 38(2) of the Land Acquisition Act 1966`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29E(1) the Court of Appeal may transfer the appeal to the Appellate Division` `s 29E(1) another appeal`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): inputs are the way, the ground
#ASSERT (`s 29E(2) the power in section 29E(1) may be exercised in this way` `s 29E(2)(a) on its own motion` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29E(2) the power in section 29E(1) may be exercised in this way` `s 29E(2)(b) on an application by a party to the appeal` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29E(2) the power in section 29E(1) may be exercised in this way` `s 29E(2)(b) on an application by a party to the appeal` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3)
#ASSERT (`s 29E(3) the Court of Appeal is to have regard to the matter` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29E(3) the Court of Appeal is to have regard to the matter` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 29E(3) the Court of Appeal is to have regard to the matter` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4), (5)
#ASSERT (`s 29E(4) the Rules of Court may prescribe different matters for the circumstance` `s 29E(2)(a) on its own motion`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29E(4) the Rules of Court may prescribe different matters for the circumstance` `s 29E(2)(b) on an application by a party to the appeal`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29E(5) the appeal may be transferred under section 29E(1) even though it was made in accordance with section 29C(2)` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 29E(5) the appeal may be transferred under section 29E(1) even though it was made in accordance with section 29C(2)` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

